    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="0443" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.51/1632.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Russell</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-04T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 4, 1915—4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Before considering increase of indebtedness to convention fund and proposed loan
                    or any non-constructive measures which would afford but temporary relief, the
                    Department will await a report of your efforts to obtain revised convention
                    contemplated in instruction No. 139 of September 17, which was drawn solely with
                    a view to assist the Dominican Government in devising some means to provide
                    permanent financial relief, to improve present unsatisfactory land <pb
                        facs="0444" n="328" xml:id="pg328"/> laws, and to preserve public order so
                    as to secure Dominicans in the peaceful development of the vast natural
                    resources of their country.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
